<text text-anchor="middle" x="804.5" y="-169.8" font-family="Open Sans" font-size="14.00">ASM&#45;100: It is assumed that the actuators</text>
<text text-anchor="middle" x="804.5" y="-154.8" font-family="Open Sans" font-size="14.00">(ESC, Servo) have their own internal</text>
<text text-anchor="middle" x="804.5" y="-139.8" font-family="Open Sans" font-size="14.00">fail&#45;safe behavior (e.g., PWM signal</text>
<text text-anchor="middle" x="804.5" y="-124.8" font-family="Open Sans" font-size="14.00">= 0% results in safe stop) that will</text>
<text text-anchor="middle" x="804.5" y="-109.8" font-family="Open Sans" font-size="14.00">be executed if the STM32 stops transmitting</text>
<text text-anchor="middle" x="804.5" y="-94.8" font-family="Open Sans" font-size="14.00">PWM due to a fault. </text>
</g>
